                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There have been 3 Football games (American football) that I have played in VR.  Each brings something different to the table.  2MD VR Football has the worst name, but is bar none the best football game in VR.  There is VR Sports Challenge on the Oculus store that has the best graphics, but is more of a mini-game than a full-fledges game.  And then there is VR QB which came out just a bit before 2MD VR football.  How does it stack up?\n\nWell, not as good as the other two options, unfortunately.  However, it still brings a nice challenge.  It has 3 different modes (classic, 2 minute drill, and scramble) and each mode has either arcade or routes format.  You can go from easy, normal, or hard.  Hard is a difficult challenge to master.  You fight for trophies and leaderboard bragging rights.  \n\nThe game will try your patience.  Try hitting a go or fly route that goes for 40 yards.  Even a 10 yard out route is difficult to hit.  And the moving targets in the endzone will try your patience.  I enjoyed scramble mode the best with route combinations in normal difficulty.  I think that mode is the best for feeling like you might actually be playing foootball.  You have to move and hit a moving target that's running a predetermined route.  \n\nSo just because I ranked this game third, doesn't mean it's bad.  In fact, your'e getting your money's worth with this game if you think you might enjoy throwing the old football around.  Best experienced in 10 minute intervals.  \n\nRating 6/10 a game to play when you have a few minutes to waste, we all need at least a few of those in our VR library",
